  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In ozone due to resonating structures O - O bond lengths are same<br />&nbsp;</p><p><img height=\"89\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7d6ef4de-b27e-46d1-b4c5-41c4c01cccc9-image.png\" width=\"314\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br />O-O bond lengths are equal is correct<br /><math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo>&#10230;</mo> <mn>3</mn> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <mn>6</mn> <mn>8&#160;</mn> <mtext>Kcal</mtext> </mrow> </math><br />It is exothermic decomposition (O<sub>3</sub> unstable). Thermal decomposition of O<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;is endothermic is wrong<br />O<sub>3</sub> is diamagnetic in nature &nbsp; Is correct due to all paired electrons.<br />O<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;has a bent structure&nbsp; Is correct with a bond angle of 116.8<sup>o</sup> and bent structure</p>",
    "image": null
